From a554572c14f4d5eac9e08f64795a60de23212671 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wang Emma <wangzhn>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:21:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] feat(cli): make --settings, tool and MCP flags take
 effect

--settings, --allowed-tools, --disallowed-tools and --mcp-config were
declared on the main command but never used. In print mode,
--permission-mode and --append-system-prompt were accepted but not passed
to build_runtime either.

- config/cli_overlay.py parses the flags into a SettingsOverlay.
  --settings is inline JSON or a path, applied as an RFC 7386 merge patch
  over settings.json. The tool flags extend the permission allow/deny
  lists. --mcp-config takes {"mcpServers": ...} or {"mcp_servers": ...}
  and replaces same-name servers. Bad input exits before the session
  starts.
- load_settings(overlay=...) applies the overlay. RuntimeBundle keeps it,
  so current_settings() and runtime refreshes preserve it. It is never
  saved to settings.json.
- Print mode, task worker and backend host now pass permission_mode,
  append_system_prompt and the overlay to build_runtime. The React
  launcher forwards the raw flags to its backend process.
- append_system_prompt is a Settings field, appended as the last
  system-prompt section. Dry-run previously replaced the base prompt;
  it now uses the same path.
- The dry-run preview shows the effective permission rules.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
